<div class="content speaker">

<h1>Adrianna Tan</h1>
<p class="speaker-lede">Founder, AI safety researcher, and product leader. I speak about building AI and civic technology that works across languages, cultures, and the public it actually serves.</p>

<div class="about-img">
<img src="/img/2024-me-square.jpg" alt="Adrianna Tan holding a Hasselblad camera and smiling">
</div>

<p>I'm the founder of <a href="https://futureethics.ai">Future Ethics</a>, an AI lab in San Francisco focused on procurement and multilingual safety standards. Before that I was AI Red Team Lead at <a href="https://www.humane-intelligence.org/">Humane Intelligence</a>, where I led large-scale evaluations — including a crowdsourced medical chatbot pilot with 200+ healthcare professionals that surfaced 800+ vulnerabilities, and a multilingual AI safety project with IMDA Singapore across 9 countries and 9 languages.</p>

<p>I've founded a venture-backed startup, led product for the City and County of San Francisco and the Monterey Bay Aquarium, and shipped Covid-19 vaccine search to millions of residents. I've spoken on stages and podcasts across more than a dozen countries, and I've been publishing on the open web since 2003.</p>

<hr>

<h2>What I speak about</h2>

<ul class="speaker-topics">
<li><strong>AI safety and red-teaming</strong> — what it actually takes to evaluate models for bias and harm, especially outside English.</li>
<li><strong>Multilingual and multicultural AI</strong> — why safety standards built for one language and culture fail everyone else, and what to do about it.</li>
<li><strong>Civic and government technology</strong> — shipping public services that millions of people depend on, and the realities of building inside government.</li>
<li><strong>Founding and product leadership</strong> — going from a startup in Southeast Asia to public service in the US, and what carries over.</li>
<li><strong>The web, identity, and the long now</strong> — queerness, immigration, and twenty-plus years of writing in public.</li>
</ul>

<p>Talks can be tuned for technical audiences, policy and procurement audiences, or general ones. <a href="/contact">Get in touch</a> to talk about a fit.</p>

